  "authoredFrom": [
    "Written by hand from decisions H3-H9, H13 and H14 (concept.md, ET-015b), docs/trips.md (One-second sampler) and the simulator clocks in docs/simulator-v1.md: the source clock is 1,000,000,000,000 ns + atMs x 1,000,000 and UTC labels are 1,800,000,000,000 ms + atMs, so the source second of a reading is 1000 + floor(atMs / 1000). A snapshot is written at its frame, at most every 50 ms after the previous state message, and carries the state published at its frame's frame_end with that frame's UTC label; a checkpoint carries the last published state at the connect time.",
    "Events: truck (1), trailer (2), job with cargo loaded (3) and simulation.started (4) at 10-40 ms, simulation.paused (5) at 5,900, simulation.started (6) at 9,000, job.delivered (7) at 16,500 and the job clear (8) at 16,510. The job opens trip@3 when it is committed (opened at load, T12), before the first snapshot in the FIFO; the delivery closes it before the snapshot at 17,000.",
    "Base transport: connection 1 from 0 to 13,000 ms, connection 2 from 15,500 to 17,500 ms, one service. Its checkpoint at 0 is the plugin session's baseline (H4). Seconds: 1000-1002 driving (the first fresh running reading of each second: frames at 100, 1,100 and 2,100); 1003-1005 at the road stop, speed 0 (3,000, 4,000, 5,000; REG-001); no row for 1006-1008, where every frame reports simulation paused, and no catch-up after the resume (REG-002); 1009 (9,000, the frame right after simulation.started); 1010 once for the twenty 50 ms frames from 10,000 to 10,950; 1011 (11,000) and 1012 (12,200; the frame at 11,600 is in second 1011); the forward game-time jump at 12,600 adds no row; no row for 1013-1014 while disconnected (REG-003); 1015 from the reconnection's checkpoint, whose SDK boundary advanced (capture 15,500, UTC label of the frame at 15,250); 1016 (16,000) still in trip@3; 1017 (17,000) after the delivery, with no trip (H7).",
    "Values are the wire's canonical units (H14): speed m/s, fuel L, average consumption 0.375 L/km x 100 = 37.5 L/100 km, estimated range and odometer km x 1,000 = m, rpm, gear index, game minutes on game-clock-0 and the position from world.placement. Every channel keeps its last value between frames.",
    "restartSamples (restartAfter [0], connection 1 from 0 to 12,300 ms, connection 2 from 12,400 to 17,500 ms): the first service stores 1000-1012 as above at its stop. The second service's checkpoint at 12,400 is its baseline, and its frame at 12,600 is sampled again as second 1012, which storage skips as already stored (H6): one skipped row, no duplicate. It then stores 1013 (13,250), 1014 (14,000), 1015 (15,000), 1016 (16,000) in the trip it resumed from the stored seed, and 1017 (17,000) without a trip."
  ],
